    "hints": [
      "Connect the primary database to a replica, and the fleet to the replica: reads go to replicas, orders to the primary.",
      "One replica might not be enough. Each replica also replays every write."
    ],
    "act": 4,
    "seed": 1041,
    "walkthrough": {
      "steps": [
        "Add two read replicas (db.t3.medium is enough).",
        "Connect the orders database to each replica, so they receive every change.",
        "Connect the web fleet to both replicas. Keep the fleet’s connection to the primary: orders still go there.",
        "Run the day. Reads now go to the replicas and the primary only handles orders."
      ],
      "why": "Product browsing is most of the database work. Two small replicas share all the reads, while the primary handles writes at about 40% load. That costs less than jumping to a db.r6g.large, which is what upgrading the one database would take."
    }
