      "sustainability": 0.5
    },
    "hints": [
      "During the warm-up nearly every read misses. Put two replicas behind the cache to absorb it.",
      "Give the fleet headroom: a lower target and a higher maximum."
    ],
    "act": 4,
    "seed": 1045,
    "walkthrough": {
      "steps": [
        "Build CloudFront → S3 for images (1-day cache).",
        "Add an ALB and an Auto Scaling Group: c7g.large, min 2, max 14, target 50%, two AZs, alarms on.",
        "Add a db.r6g.large orders database, plus two db.r6g.large read replicas connected from it.",
        "Add ElastiCache (TTL 5 minutes). Connect fleet → cache → both replicas, and fleet → database for orders.",
        "Run the day and watch 9:00: the cache is empty just as traffic quadruples."
      ],
      "why": "For the first 20 minutes after the flush nearly every read misses the cache. Two large replicas behind the cache absorb that stampede. The fleet’s 50% target leaves headroom while new instances boot. After warm-up the cache takes most reads again, and staleness stays within 5 minutes."
    }
